---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/urls';
---

<Page
  article
  title="About MutualLens"
  description="MutualLens helps you compare Instagram followers and following, understand the results, and keep uploaded files on your device."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE PROJECT</p><h1>Clarity over assumptions.</h1><p
    class="lede"
  >
    MutualLens is a project by Arhaan Aggarwal, built to make follower and
    following comparisons readable and explain what the data can actually
    support.
  </p>
  <h2>A useful view of your connections</h2><p>
    Upload your Instagram relationship files to see who does not follow you
    back, your mutual followers, and who you do not follow back. Search the
    lists, download the results, or choose to save a snapshot in your browser.
  </p>
  <h2>Context with every comparison</h2><p>
    Reports describe the files you provide. They do not claim to show live
    Instagram activity or explain why someone’s relationship with your account
    changed. Missing parts and unreadable records are called out alongside the
    affected results.
  </p>
  <h2>Readable by design</h2><p>
    The interface emphasizes lists, meaningful labels, and provenance. It avoids
    remote avatars, social embeds, and decorative profile lookups. Results
    describe supplied relationships without assigning motives or automating
    unfollows.
  </p>
  <p>
    Source code and development progress are available in the <a
      href="https://github.com/Arhaan2/mutuallens"
      target="_blank"
      rel="noopener noreferrer">MutualLens GitHub repository</a
    >. MutualLens is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or operated by Instagram
    or Meta.
  </p>
  <p>
    <a href={sitePath('/guides/')}>Browse the practical guides</a> or <a
      href={sitePath('/')}>return to the checker overview</a
    >.
  </p>
</Page>
